@startuml
title User Registration and Authentication Sequence with JWT

actor User
participant "Angular SPA" as SPA
participant "AuthService" as AuthService
participant "AuthController" as API
participant "JWT Service" as JWTService
participant "User Database" as DB

== User Registration ==
User -> SPA : Submit registration form
SPA -> AuthService : register(userData)
AuthService -> API : POST /api/auth/register
activate API
API -> DB : Create user record
API -> JWTService : Generate JWT tokens
JWTService --> API : Return access & refresh tokens
API --> AuthService : 200 OK with tokens
deactivate API
AuthService -> SPA : Store tokens in localStorage
SPA --> User : Registration successful

== User Login ==
User -> SPA : Submit login form
SPA -> AuthService : login(credentials)
AuthService -> API : POST /api/auth/login
activate API
API -> DB : Validate credentials
API -> JWTService : Generate JWT tokens
JWTService --> API : Return access & refresh tokens
API --> AuthService : 200 OK with tokens
deactivate API
AuthService -> SPA : Store tokens in localStorage
SPA --> User : Login successful

== Token Refresh ==
SPA -> AuthService : Token expired, refresh needed
AuthService -> API : POST /api/auth/refresh
activate API
API -> JWTService : Validate refresh token
JWTService --> API : Return new access token
API --> AuthService : 200 OK with new access token
deactivate API
AuthService -> SPA : Update access token
SPA -> API : Continue with new token

== Protected API Request ==
SPA -> AuthService : Make authenticated request
AuthService -> API : GET /api/protected (with Authorization header)
activate API
API -> API : Validate JWT token
API --> AuthService : 200 OK with data
deactivate API
AuthService -> SPA : Return data
SPA --> User : Display data

@enduml
